 "comment": "Pattern 2, bank or cash vouchers whose narration names a party with no amount on the voucher. b01 and b02 pay Beta Stores and name Gamma Supplies (b02 also names its own party). b03 is a receipt from Alpha Traders naming Gamma Supplies and Beta Stores. b04 is a contra from Bank A to Petty Cash naming Alpha Traders (both of its lines are bank or cash, so its money counts once, as its larger side). b05 is a cash payment naming Beta Stores. b06 pays Kappa Traders and names it, but Kappa-Traders has the same words in the same order, so the name is shared and bound to no master, and b06 is not listed. b07 pays rent and names Omega Mart, a name two party masters share in different case, and Sigma Stores, a name a party and an expense master share: neither is read, so b07 is not listed. b08 names Unit 7 Supplies. b09 names Café Corner with the accent; b10 writes it without the accent, which is ignored on a letter a to z, so b10 names Café Corner too. b11's narration, in Devanagari only, names the Devanagari party देव ट्रेडर्स. b12 names Gamma Supplies, which has only a zero-amount line on it: a zero line posts nothing, so b12 is listed. b13 is booked to two ledgers and names Gamma Supplies. b14 names Alpha Traders twice. b15 pays from two bank ledgers and names Beta Stores.",
